# Only the playable game goes in the repository: the game itself (race/), the music, and
# the art it actually loads. Everything else stays local: the unused source art, the card
# and roster generators, and the dev tools (tools/dev/ holds a local test account).
/*
!/README.md
!/index.html
!/.nojekyll
!/.gitignore
!/Play Post Parade.bat
!/race/
!/audio/
# ...but not the test scripts and lab pages in race/: they run during development, not in the game
/race/validate*.js
/race/*-lab.html

# Racers/ and backgrounds/ hold far more than the game uses, so only the files it loads
# are tracked -- added by name. When the game starts loading a new one, add it with
#   git add -f "Racers/<file>"
# (it stays tracked from then on).
